From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:28:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] Lab: XCL_THREAD_SAMPLE and XCL_CALL_STATS - where the
 CPU time goes, without elevation

XCL_THREAD_SAMPLE=<from s>,<period ms>,<count> (+ XCL_THREAD_SAMPLE_FILE): every period, each
other thread's cycle time (QueryThreadCycleTime) and, when it ran, its RIP and up to 7 return
addresses (stopped only for GetThreadContext and a 16 KiB stack copy, unwound afterwards from the
copy with RtlVirtualUnwind); a thread that did not run and waits in ntdll / win32u is not stopped.
Written to a binary file with the modules (full paths) and thread names; counts in the log.

XCL_CALL_STATS=1[,<s>]: calls and time by kind of the Win32 / D3D12 calls around the title's
submits (write watch, VirtualQuery / VirtualProtect, ReadProcessMemory, Map / Unmap, fences,
queue Signal / Wait, UpdateTileMappings, XCL's copy recordings, ECLs, STATE / TEXTURES / REFRESH
lock waits) and timers over the parts of the submit hook and of the refresh; totals in the log.

Both off unless set. No translator source touched (identity 793bcfdace7b0c74).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
